92e43879-f0f0-4e7e-8d25-723783305410	c6a25b61-c886-4677-9de2-4bf7b6891acd	\N	Other	Dear Dailymeat Support Team,\n\nI am receiving multiple OTP messages from Dailymeat within a span of just a few minutes, despite already having the Dailymeat app installed and an existing account registered with my mobile number.\n\nI have not initiated any registration or login requests. This raises concerns that someone may be repeatedly attempting to use my mobile number or deliberately triggering OTP requests.\n\nPlease investigate this issue immediately, check the source of these OTP requests, and take necessary action to prevent further unauthorised attempts.\n\nKindly confirm whether there have been any login or registration attempts using my mobile number without my knowledge.\n\nI request you to treat this as a security concern and provide an early resolution.\n\nRegards\nIliyaz \n	RESOLVED	Dear Iliyaz,\n\nThank you for contacting DailyMeat Support and for reporting this to us.\n\nWe sincerely apologise for the repeated OTP messages you received. The issue was caused by a fault on our SMS provider's side, which triggered OTP messages to be sent repeatedly. It was not caused by any login or registration attempt made by you or by anyone else using your mobile number.\n\nThe issue has now been resolved, and you will not receive these messages again. Please ignore the OTPs you received and do not share them with anyone. Your existing account and the DailyMeat app can be used as usual.\n\nWe are also putting additional safeguards in place so that this kind of error does not happen again.\n\nWe apologise for the inconvenience and appreciate your patience and understanding. If you notice anything unusual again, please reply to this support ticket, otherwise resolved from your end kindly close the ticket.\n\nRegards,\nDailyMeat Support Team	2026-11-11 17:34:51.414+00	2026-11-11 10:32:19.675+00	2026-11-11 17:34:51.414+00
\.
